      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60cb1fb048ea0a340b54e3d7|full_name}: There was discussion on discord that trackers paired to vive tracker dongles may suffer from a real-space offset, whereas devices paired to a headset's internal \"dongle\" don't suffer from this issue.\nIt would be a good idea to hold your elbow tracker in your hand simultaneously while holding your hand controller and spin around IRL while observing the render models of those devices in the SteamVR overlay. Please report if they do or don't weave in small circles relative to each other.\nA further step in testing this would be to pair your elbow trackers to your headset, and controllers to your external dongles. Then repeat the controller-held-against-HMD 360 rotation to see if the controller now begin to weave in small circles. And then also observe if the elbow tracker asymmetry is removed when those trackers are paired to the HMD.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
